1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,660
What the hell were you thinking, Mr. Westcott?

2
00:00:06,880 --> 00:00:08,260
Please do enlighten us.

3
00:00:08,540 --> 00:00:11,960
Sorry, I'm not quite sure what you're asking, Murdoch.

4
00:00:12,200 --> 00:00:13,880
Now's not the time to play dumb.

5
00:00:14,240 --> 00:00:17,420
I'm obviously referring to your many recent activities in Japan.

6
00:00:18,040 --> 00:00:19,680
Interfering with the self-defense force,

7
00:00:19,960 --> 00:00:21,580
utilizing wizards for your own agenda,

8
00:00:21,960 --> 00:00:24,820
and worse, transforming the city into a war zone.

9
00:00:25,380 --> 00:00:27,700
The Japanese government is all over us thanks to you.

10
00:00:27,700 --> 00:00:30,480
How do you plan to rectify this mess?

11
00:00:31,020 --> 00:00:32,100
Look, what does it matter?

12
00:00:32,420 --> 00:00:34,760
We obviously achieved enough to make it worthwhile.

13
00:00:35,140 --> 00:00:37,840
Don't forget, we succeeded with Princess's inversion.

14
00:00:38,120 --> 00:00:40,480
Do you really not understand what I'm saying?

15
00:00:40,980 --> 00:00:41,800
It's ludicrous.

16
00:00:42,060 --> 00:00:44,680
What do spirits have to do with saving D.E.M.?

17
00:00:44,680 --> 00:00:48,160
The company can't afford to take a backseat to your selfish little obsessions.

18
00:00:48,640 --> 00:00:50,720
Everyone, I think the time has come.

19
00:00:50,920 --> 00:00:54,320
I move that managing director Westcott be relieved of his position.

20
00:00:54,320 --> 00:00:57,640
Are you willing to comply with this, sir?

21
00:00:57,840 --> 00:00:58,400
Of course.

22
00:00:59,060 --> 00:01:02,320
Removing me is well within your given rights as the board of directors.

23
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:06,920
Well then, Chairman Russell, I say we proceed with a vote right now.

24
00:01:07,680 --> 00:01:08,240
All right.

25
00:01:08,520 --> 00:01:10,960
All those in favor of Westcott's dismissal.

26
00:01:14,300 --> 00:01:15,420
Zero hands.

27
00:01:15,640 --> 00:01:17,260
His removal is hereby rejected.

28
00:01:17,540 --> 00:01:17,860
What?

29
00:01:18,060 --> 00:01:19,620
What are you talking about, Chairman?

30
00:01:19,620 --> 00:01:21,300
All these people agree with me.

31
00:01:26,580 --> 00:01:29,160
You'll find realizers ready at the infirmary.

32
00:01:29,500 --> 00:01:33,320
If you get there fast, you should be back to normal in a few days.

33
00:01:35,620 --> 00:01:39,000
And once I'm finished addressing my selfish little obsession,

34
00:01:39,260 --> 00:01:40,840
I shall hand over the company.

35
00:01:41,480 --> 00:01:41,800
Soon.

36
00:01:42,040 --> 00:01:42,600
Don't worry.

37
00:01:42,600 --> 00:01:46,280
At least compared to how long we've already been waiting, anyway.

38
00:01:51,340 --> 00:01:53,100
A written challenge.

39
00:01:53,820 --> 00:01:56,160
And with it, 12 photographs.

40
00:01:57,180 --> 00:01:58,120
For one question,

41
00:01:59,180 --> 00:02:00,540
can you find me?

42
00:02:00,540 --> 00:02:01,760
Don't worry.

43
00:02:13,560 --> 00:02:18,020
Okay.

44
00:02:18,020 --> 00:02:48,000
Thank you.

45
00:02:48,020 --> 00:03:18,000
Thank you.

46
00:03:18,020 --> 00:03:20,020
Thank you.

47
00:03:48,020 --> 00:03:50,020
Thank you.

48
00:04:18,880 --> 00:04:19,800
That's true.

49
00:04:20,080 --> 00:04:21,740
She seems different from Kurumi.

50
00:04:22,240 --> 00:04:26,300
I have a feeling Natsumi may not be satisfied playing around and keeping it light.

51
00:04:26,820 --> 00:04:30,340
The fact is, someone here may already be gone for eternity.

52
00:04:30,340 --> 00:04:32,960
No, I don't think Natsumi is like that.

53
00:04:33,300 --> 00:04:37,720
If I can just guess who she's impersonating, I know they'll come home in one piece.

54
00:04:38,280 --> 00:04:40,780
Sounds like you're putting a lot of faith in this witch.

55
00:04:41,620 --> 00:04:42,560
Think about it.

56
00:04:42,700 --> 00:04:46,180
Could you open up your heart to someone if you didn't think they trusted you?

57
00:04:46,180 --> 00:04:50,260
As if you know women at all.

58
00:04:50,840 --> 00:04:53,180
Though, I will admit that was accurate.

59
00:04:53,740 --> 00:04:54,140
Mm-hmm.

60
00:04:54,700 --> 00:04:56,540
Whatever the case, we need to hurry.

61
00:04:57,400 --> 00:04:58,080
Sorry, Coterie.

62
00:04:58,480 --> 00:05:00,680
I'm afraid you'll have to stay away from command.

63
00:05:01,280 --> 00:05:02,500
Yeah, that makes sense.

64
00:05:02,740 --> 00:05:05,440
I could just as easily be Natsumi as anyone else could.

65
00:05:05,440 --> 00:05:10,080
And you, Shin, you have an awful lot of work ahead of you.

66
00:05:11,120 --> 00:05:12,620
Okay, what should I do?

67
00:05:13,240 --> 00:05:18,620
For the time being, I'd start by deciding the order you'll be dating them in.

68
00:05:21,740 --> 00:05:27,900
To see through Natsumi's disguise, be careful not to overlook even the smallest differences from the norm.

69
00:05:28,760 --> 00:05:32,160
You'll date them one by one in search of anything that seems off.

70
00:05:32,160 --> 00:05:37,180
Feels wrong somehow to go out on dates while I'm doubting everyone.

71
00:05:37,380 --> 00:05:38,780
Oh, good morning, Shido!

72
00:05:41,340 --> 00:05:43,360
I'm sorry, were you waiting long?

73
00:05:43,600 --> 00:05:45,540
Not at all. You're right on time.

74
00:05:52,120 --> 00:05:54,960
This has to be Toka. I mean, look at her.

75
00:05:56,400 --> 00:05:57,840
Is anything wrong, Shido?

76
00:05:58,120 --> 00:06:00,240
You seem a lot more quiet than usual.

77
00:06:02,160 --> 00:06:04,660
You think? No, I'm super great, really!

78
00:06:04,880 --> 00:06:06,000
Try to relax, Shin.

79
00:06:06,780 --> 00:06:08,200
Remember, she's good at this.

80
00:06:08,620 --> 00:06:10,520
You won't see through her disguise easily.

81
00:06:11,700 --> 00:06:13,360
Let's try to shake her up a bit.

82
00:06:16,360 --> 00:06:17,360
Hey, Toka.

83
00:06:17,860 --> 00:06:19,920
Would you remind me when we went out last?

84
00:06:20,100 --> 00:06:21,120
I can't remember.

85
00:06:21,900 --> 00:06:22,320
Huh?

86
00:06:22,440 --> 00:06:23,740
What are you talking about?

87
00:06:24,000 --> 00:06:26,780
Have you forgotten that we went shopping just a few days ago?

88
00:06:26,780 --> 00:06:28,700
Oh, yeah, that's right.

89
00:06:29,040 --> 00:06:29,860
She got it.

90
00:06:30,260 --> 00:06:31,300
So, what's next?

91
00:06:31,560 --> 00:06:34,360
But I don't mind going out again so soon, just so you know.

92
00:06:34,740 --> 00:06:36,960
It's one of the things that makes me the happiest.

93
00:06:37,920 --> 00:06:38,480
Toka.

94
00:06:42,620 --> 00:06:44,180
I'm totally on to you.

95
00:06:44,440 --> 00:06:44,760
Huh?

96
00:06:44,760 --> 00:06:48,000
You play Toka well, right, Natsumi?

97
00:06:51,100 --> 00:06:52,900
Wait, are you not?

98
00:06:53,340 --> 00:06:53,740
Shido?

99
00:06:54,100 --> 00:06:55,560
Who the heck is this Natsumi?

100
00:06:56,280 --> 00:06:59,420
Don't try to pretend like you didn't just blurt out another girl's name, Shido!

101
00:06:59,640 --> 00:07:02,160
You better tell me where this other girl is right now!

102
00:07:02,320 --> 00:07:03,540
No, you misunderstood.

103
00:07:03,900 --> 00:07:05,340
That's a kind of a greeting.

104
00:07:05,760 --> 00:07:09,340
It started in an island down south, and now it's caught on in Japan, too.

105
00:07:10,220 --> 00:07:10,620
Natsumi!

106
00:07:11,200 --> 00:07:11,600
Natsumi!

107
00:07:11,960 --> 00:07:12,200
See?

108
00:07:12,200 --> 00:07:13,220
Is that true?

109
00:07:14,120 --> 00:07:15,840
Wow, what an incredible lie.

110
00:07:16,160 --> 00:07:18,440
It's so bad, it almost has to be real.

111
00:07:18,820 --> 00:07:19,580
Oh, okay.

112
00:07:19,760 --> 00:07:21,280
Well, I guess that makes sense.

113
00:07:21,540 --> 00:07:24,340
So, when they use Natsumi as a greeting, what does it mean?

114
00:07:24,880 --> 00:07:28,120
Uh, well, I'm pretty sure it means I love you.

115
00:07:28,260 --> 00:07:29,420
Or something close.

116
00:07:30,040 --> 00:07:30,900
I see.

117
00:07:32,700 --> 00:07:36,180
Oh, also, what did you mean when you said I play Toka well?

118
00:07:37,760 --> 00:07:39,320
Wow, Toka, check it out!

119
00:07:39,380 --> 00:07:41,360
That restaurant is totally doing a lunch buffet!

120
00:07:41,360 --> 00:07:43,760
We have to get in there and take advantage!

121
00:07:44,520 --> 00:07:45,780
You want to get lunch?

122
00:07:45,980 --> 00:07:47,320
Sure, I mean, I could eat.

123
00:07:47,700 --> 00:07:49,640
All right, let's do it then.

124
00:07:50,920 --> 00:07:53,320
Wait a minute, what is this reaction?

125
00:07:54,140 --> 00:07:57,180
Normally, one mention of food would instantly cheer her up.

126
00:07:57,180 --> 00:08:03,040
So far, we've had no detection of Natsumi.

127
00:08:03,720 --> 00:08:05,180
How has it felt on your end?

128
00:08:05,980 --> 00:08:08,020
I'm thinking it's gotta be the real Toka.

129
00:08:08,460 --> 00:08:10,740
But we're here to eat lunch and she seems so...

130
00:08:10,740 --> 00:08:15,160
Problem?

131
00:08:15,640 --> 00:08:17,380
What, is something the matter, Shido?

132
00:08:17,800 --> 00:08:18,620
Oh, no.

133
00:08:19,280 --> 00:08:21,680
No way! Toka only filled half her plate?

134
00:08:22,340 --> 00:08:24,060
Strange. I wonder if she's sick.

135
00:08:24,200 --> 00:08:24,880
That's absurd!

136
00:08:25,120 --> 00:08:27,220
She's always a bottomless pit, no matter what!

137
00:08:27,500 --> 00:08:29,140
Hey, were you waiting for me?

138
00:08:29,140 --> 00:08:30,960
Thanks, let's eat up.

139
00:08:31,360 --> 00:08:33,060
Right. Yeah, we should.

140
00:08:35,820 --> 00:08:36,840
Is it true?

141
00:08:37,260 --> 00:08:39,180
Is Toka really not Suni?

142
00:08:39,480 --> 00:08:40,660
Thanks for the lunch.

143
00:08:41,140 --> 00:08:41,980
You're done?

144
00:08:43,700 --> 00:08:44,920
What's wrong, Toka?

145
00:08:45,420 --> 00:08:47,400
That couldn't have been enough food for you.

146
00:08:48,040 --> 00:08:49,100
No, it's okay.

147
00:08:49,100 --> 00:08:49,340
I...

148
00:08:49,340 --> 00:08:51,200
I saw something on TV.

149
00:08:51,960 --> 00:08:53,100
You have to be careful.

150
00:08:53,400 --> 00:08:55,260
Girls who regularly eat a lot more than guys

151
00:08:55,260 --> 00:08:57,020
can sometimes be a real turn-off.

152
00:08:59,080 --> 00:09:00,300
See, the thing is,

153
00:09:00,360 --> 00:09:02,160
I didn't want you to be turned off by me,

154
00:09:02,220 --> 00:09:04,160
so I thought I would eat less.

155
00:09:04,580 --> 00:09:05,060
Actually,

156
00:09:05,460 --> 00:09:07,420
I really prefer girls who are happy

157
00:09:07,420 --> 00:09:08,940
to scarf down lots of food.

158
00:09:09,780 --> 00:09:10,920
Do you mean it?

159
00:09:13,040 --> 00:09:15,300
Yeah, it's definitely Toka.

160
00:09:15,600 --> 00:09:16,040
Fine.

161
00:09:16,320 --> 00:09:18,420
But we still can't dismiss her just yet.

162
00:09:18,420 --> 00:09:20,880
Stay with Toka and let her finish eating.

163
00:09:21,360 --> 00:09:22,960
But make sure to get back home

164
00:09:22,960 --> 00:09:24,260
by at least 3 o'clock.

165
00:09:25,020 --> 00:09:26,740
Your next date will come over

166
00:09:26,740 --> 00:09:27,540
and meet you there.

167
00:09:32,380 --> 00:09:32,900
Yep!

168
00:09:33,060 --> 00:09:34,020
Hang on, I'm coming!

169
00:09:34,860 --> 00:09:35,340
Boo!

170
00:09:35,700 --> 00:09:36,060
Ah!

171
00:09:38,780 --> 00:09:39,260
Ah!

172
00:09:39,920 --> 00:09:41,660
Might want to be more careful, Shido.

173
00:09:42,440 --> 00:09:43,580
Uh, right, thanks.

174
00:09:43,840 --> 00:09:45,760
I just wasn't expecting to see you.

175
00:09:46,120 --> 00:09:48,400
Then I guess today's your lucky day!

176
00:09:49,400 --> 00:09:50,140
Oh, man.

177
00:09:50,860 --> 00:09:52,480
Sorry about that, Yoshino.

178
00:09:53,100 --> 00:09:55,100
Yoshinan kind of surprised me.

179
00:09:58,460 --> 00:10:00,360
Ah, trick-or-treat.

180
00:10:01,360 --> 00:10:03,260
If you don't give me any candy,

181
00:10:03,620 --> 00:10:05,320
I think I have to prank you.

182
00:10:05,320 --> 00:10:15,860
Shido, this is so...

183
00:10:15,860 --> 00:10:16,780
I have to say,

184
00:10:16,860 --> 00:10:18,740
I never thought you'd come here trick-or-treating.

185
00:10:19,020 --> 00:10:20,340
Afraid we're all out of candy.

186
00:10:21,100 --> 00:10:22,880
I hope the hotcakes will do.

187
00:10:24,640 --> 00:10:26,180
This is a first for me.

188
00:10:26,280 --> 00:10:27,340
I've never had them.

189
00:10:27,740 --> 00:10:28,300
I see.

190
00:10:28,300 --> 00:10:29,840
Well, I hope you enjoy.

191
00:10:29,840 --> 00:10:46,820
You had the same reaction

192
00:10:46,820 --> 00:10:48,660
the first time you came here, remember?

193
00:10:49,400 --> 00:10:50,380
Let me see.

194
00:10:50,880 --> 00:10:53,100
Remind me what it was you ate that day.

195
00:10:53,980 --> 00:10:55,160
Oh, what was it?

196
00:10:59,940 --> 00:11:00,620
That's right.

197
00:11:00,700 --> 00:11:02,180
You made Oyakodan for me.

198
00:11:02,500 --> 00:11:03,300
Ah, yes.

199
00:11:03,320 --> 00:11:03,940
That was it.

200
00:11:04,320 --> 00:11:06,520
Oh, what are you talking about, Shido?

201
00:11:07,040 --> 00:11:08,540
That doesn't ring a bell to me.

202
00:11:08,760 --> 00:11:09,620
You don't remember?

203
00:11:10,540 --> 00:11:10,940
No.

204
00:11:11,700 --> 00:11:12,720
I wonder, though.

205
00:11:12,780 --> 00:11:13,740
Do you think it could have been

206
00:11:13,740 --> 00:11:14,380
during that time

207
00:11:14,380 --> 00:11:16,080
when I stayed over at Origami's?

208
00:11:16,180 --> 00:11:16,840
Oh, yeah.

209
00:11:16,900 --> 00:11:18,140
I forgot that ever happened.

210
00:11:18,820 --> 00:11:20,820
I actually had to invade Origami's place

211
00:11:20,820 --> 00:11:22,100
to get you back, didn't I?

212
00:11:22,360 --> 00:11:22,660
Oh, sure.

213
00:11:23,380 --> 00:11:23,820
Huh?

214
00:11:24,280 --> 00:11:26,680
Come on, just do it.

215
00:11:27,640 --> 00:11:28,860
What would you think

216
00:11:28,860 --> 00:11:30,920
about sharing this with me?

217
00:11:31,580 --> 00:11:32,600
No, that's okay.

218
00:11:32,600 --> 00:11:34,780
I mean, I made those especially for you.

219
00:11:37,100 --> 00:11:38,720
Oh, all right, fine.

220
00:11:38,800 --> 00:11:39,360
We can share.

221
00:11:39,560 --> 00:11:40,400
Give me a bite.

222
00:11:41,320 --> 00:11:42,360
Say, ah.

223
00:11:43,600 --> 00:11:43,960
Ah.

224
00:11:46,800 --> 00:11:48,020
Isn't that yummy?

225
00:11:48,780 --> 00:11:49,140
Mm-hmm.

226
00:11:49,300 --> 00:11:50,440
It really is.

227
00:11:52,780 --> 00:11:54,720
Shido, you've got a little syrup.

228
00:11:55,100 --> 00:11:55,300
Huh?

229
00:11:55,720 --> 00:11:56,600
Where is it?

230
00:12:01,880 --> 00:12:02,360
Whoa!

231
00:12:03,960 --> 00:12:05,280
Hot cakes are, like,

232
00:12:05,560 --> 00:12:07,920
halfway between a food and a candy, actually.

233
00:12:08,560 --> 00:12:10,880
So that's why, why I just...

234
00:12:10,880 --> 00:12:12,220
It was just a prank, okay?

235
00:12:13,920 --> 00:12:15,020
Whoa, whoa!

236
00:12:15,200 --> 00:12:16,140
You go, girl!

237
00:12:16,760 --> 00:12:17,660
Hey, Reina,

238
00:12:17,900 --> 00:12:20,380
I think that was the real Yoshino,

239
00:12:20,540 --> 00:12:21,000
don't you?

240
00:12:21,540 --> 00:12:22,900
Well, who knows, really.

241
00:12:23,880 --> 00:12:26,020
So, who's up next on the agenda?

242
00:12:26,420 --> 00:12:26,760
Right.

243
00:12:27,440 --> 00:12:27,900
Hirito,

244
00:12:28,220 --> 00:12:28,760
Tonomachi.

245
00:12:32,120 --> 00:12:32,600
Toka,

246
00:12:33,120 --> 00:12:33,580
Yoshino,

247
00:12:33,940 --> 00:12:34,680
and Tonomachi.

248
00:12:35,360 --> 00:12:36,360
We're three dates down

249
00:12:36,360 --> 00:12:37,320
with no real leads

250
00:12:37,320 --> 00:12:38,280
on what we're looking for.

251
00:12:38,920 --> 00:12:39,700
None of their behavior

252
00:12:39,700 --> 00:12:40,600
seemed any different

253
00:12:40,600 --> 00:12:41,980
than usual to any of us.

254
00:12:41,980 --> 00:12:43,400
I'd prefer not to call

255
00:12:43,400 --> 00:12:43,920
that whole thing

256
00:12:43,920 --> 00:12:45,000
with Tonomachi a date,

257
00:12:45,060 --> 00:12:45,640
if that's okay.

258
00:12:46,680 --> 00:12:47,040
Shin,

259
00:12:47,440 --> 00:12:48,680
think you can handle one more?

260
00:12:49,420 --> 00:12:50,960
Yuzuru is already waiting for you

261
00:12:50,960 --> 00:12:52,240
at the designated location.

262
00:12:52,940 --> 00:12:53,420
Absolutely.

263
00:12:55,620 --> 00:12:56,680
Sorry, Yuzuru.

264
00:12:57,040 --> 00:12:57,520
Offended.

265
00:12:58,080 --> 00:12:59,540
Some nerve inviting me here

266
00:12:59,540 --> 00:13:00,460
and arriving late.

267
00:13:00,620 --> 00:13:01,700
What do you have to say?

268
00:13:02,080 --> 00:13:02,900
So sorry.

269
00:13:03,060 --> 00:13:04,340
I was running a bit behind.

270
00:13:05,860 --> 00:13:06,260
Pardoned.

271
00:13:06,660 --> 00:13:07,440
It's all right.

272
00:13:07,920 --> 00:13:09,480
You'll find I have a big heart,

273
00:13:09,660 --> 00:13:11,040
so we will just call

274
00:13:11,040 --> 00:13:11,820
those five minutes

275
00:13:11,820 --> 00:13:12,460
an anomaly.

276
00:13:15,760 --> 00:13:20,760
Are you unhappy

277
00:13:20,760 --> 00:13:22,080
that I'm the only one here?

278
